Changes applied to MagiAttention (https://github.com/SandAI-org/MagiAttention) @ a3276e7b for the evaluation:
- functional/dist_attn.py, dist_attn_runtime_mgr.py: MAGI_ATTENTION_BACKWARD_HIGH_PRECISION_REDUCE=1 is honoured
  with the FA4 kernel backend (partial dQ / dK / dV widened to fp32 before the group reduce; fp32 buffers).
- utils/dtype.py: no fp4 dtype on PyTorch 2.5.
Install the patched tree (pip install --no-build-isolation .) so the imported copy is the patched one.

diff --git a/magi_attention/dist_attn_runtime_mgr.py b/magi_attention/dist_attn_runtime_mgr.py
index b56c5bd..16e652f 100644
--- a/magi_attention/dist_attn_runtime_mgr.py
+++ b/magi_attention/dist_attn_runtime_mgr.py
@@ -475,8 +475,9 @@ def check_flag_comb() -> None:
 
         assert (  # TODO
             not env.comm.is_fwd_high_precision_reduce_enable()
-            and not env.comm.is_bwd_high_precision_reduce_enable()
-        ), "FA4 backend is not compatible with high-precision reduce for now"
+            # backward high-precision reduce is implemented for FA4 in functional/dist_attn.py (FA4's per-call
+            # partial dq / dk / dv widened to fp32), so only the forward is refused
+        ), "FA4 backend is not compatible with forward high-precision reduce for now"
 
         assert (  # TODO
             not env.comm.is_qo_comm_enable()
